<title>POLAND: Polish food prices rise 0.3 pct in Dec 10-20.</title>
<headline>Polish food prices rise 0.3 pct in Dec 10-20.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 0.3 percent in the December 10-20 period after rising 1.9 percent in the previous 10 days and were 2.3 percent higher than in the November 10-20 period, the Central Statistical Office said.</p>
<p>				   DEC 10-20    DEC 1-10   LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p> POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)     0.3	   1.9	  2.3 (2.2)</p>
<p> Bread				0.2	   0.0	  0.6 (0.6)</p>
<p> Fruit and vegetables	   1.4	  17.1	19.7 (18.5)</p>
<p> Meat and meat-products	-0.1	  -0.3	 -0.7(-0.7)</p>
<p> Dairy products		   0.5	   0.7	  1.5 (1.2)</p>
<p> Eggs				 0.6	   0.7	  2.0 (1.9)</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in brackets are for the 30-day period ended December 10 -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
